    colors: each object has a distinct non-bg color
    bbox_width: 2-6 columns; must be >= 2 (solver asserts)
    bbox_height: 2-5 rows
    pixel_count: 4-14
    shapes: arbitrary 4-connected blobs; no symmetry requirement
    separation: min Chebyshev distance >= 2 between any two objects (no 8-adjacency)
    bg_fraction: ~55-70% of grid is background
  transform:
    for each object, erase (set to bg) all pixels in the 2 leftmost columns of its bounding box
    0-1 objects may be fully erased (bbox_width == 2) per example [observed]

generation_strategy:
  approach: direct construction (transform is simple column-erasure, no inversion needed)
  steps:
    1. Pick grid size H x W in [8,11].
    2. Fill grid with bg color. Pick 4 distinct non-bg colors.
    3. For each object, generate a random 4-connected blob with bbox_width in [2,6], bbox_height in [2,5], pixel_count in [4,14]. Ensure blob has at least some pixels in its 2 leftmost bbox columns.
    4. Place objects on the grid with min Chebyshev gap >= 2 between all pairs; reject/retry placement on collision. Ensure objects stay within grid bounds.
    5. Verify bg fraction is >= 50%.
    6. Output is computed by erasing (setting to bg) each object's pixels in its 2 leftmost bbox columns.

